Subject: drivers loaded at boot register their majors; ddi and str on the host

A driver loaded at boot or by modload found no slot: only a demand-class
registration or modadmin -r made one, so its linkage failed with EINVAL
(S3-B5 on k30: z3660eth, "error 22").  drv_install now registers the
module's own registry majors, dlm_sreg for a STREAMS driver and dlm_creg
otherwise; a STREAMS driver in demand class is refused with a console
line.  The state harness builds dlm_str.c and dlm_ddi.c (host stand-ins
for sys/stream.h and sys/conf.h, a run-address accessor for the ifstats
list) and gains boot-class driver cases and ifstats backstop cases: the
module's link first, in the middle and last, after a failed _load, after
an _unload that forgot, and after a failed linkage.

